---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout pageType="article" title="BSFC Explained" description="What brake-specific fuel consumption measures, why it varies, and how it affects injector sizing.">
  <article class="guide-page">
    <header>
      <h1>BSFC Explained</h1>
      <p class="guide-meta">Brake-specific fuel consumption — what it is, why it varies, and injector sizing</p>
    </header>
    <section>
      <h2>What BSFC Measures</h2>
      <p>Brake-specific fuel consumption is fuel mass flow divided by measured brake power at the same operating point. Units must stay consistent.</p>
      <p class="formula-inline">BSFC = fuel mass flow (lb/hr) / power (hp)</p>
      <p>For example, 200 lb/hr divided by 400 hp gives 0.50 lb/(hp·hr). Convert to g/(kW·hr) by multiplying by 453.59237 and dividing by 0.745699872: approximately 304 g/(kW·hr).</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Choosing an Assumption</h2>
      <p>BSFC depends on fuel, load, RPM, and engine calibration. A measured fuel-flow and power pair is more specific than a generic engine-category range. Do not treat the calculator's 0.50 default as a universal recommendation.</p>
      <p>Use appropriate engine data, record the operating point and fuel, and check your assumptions with the engine builder or tuner. A change of fuel needs an appropriate BSFC as well as density.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>How Injector Sizing Uses BSFC</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/calculators/fuel-injector/">Fuel Injector Calculator</a> multiplies target power by BSFC for required fuel mass flow, then divides by injector count and selected duty cycle.</p>
      <p class="formula-inline">flow per injector (lb/hr) = hp × BSFC / (injector count × duty cycle)</p>
      <p>For 400 hp, BSFC 0.50, four injectors, and duty cycle 0.80, the example produces 62.5 lb/hr per injector. With density 0.75 g/mL, this is approximately 630 cc/min.</p>
      <p>These are example assumptions. Duty-cycle and fuel-pressure requirements must come from the injector and system specifications.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Common Input Mistakes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Entering 80 instead of 0.80 for an 80% duty cycle.</li>
        <li>Mixing crankshaft power with BSFC measured at a different power measurement point.</li>
        <li>Changing density alone and treating it as a complete fuel conversion.</li>
        <li>Comparing injector flow ratings measured at different pressures.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Method and Manufacturer Reference</h2>
      <p><a href="https://www.holley.com/blog/post/how_to_properly_size_fuel_injectors_for_your_engine/">Holley's injector sizing explanation</a> describes the relationship between horsepower, BSFC, injector count, duty cycle, and fuel pressure. Apply the specifications for the components you actually use.</p>
      <p>See the site's <a href="/methodology/#injector">injector methodology</a> for the density conversion and the limits of the estimate.</p>
    </section>
    <nav class="guide-nav">
      <a href="/calculators/fuel-injector/" class="btn-primary">Fuel Injector Calculator</a>
      <a href="/fueling/" class="btn-secondary">Fueling Hub</a>
    </nav>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .guide-page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .guide-page header { margin-bottom: 2rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-primary); }
  .guide-page h1 { font-size: 1.75rem; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .guide-meta { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; margin: 0; }
  .guide-page h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; padding-bottom: 0.375rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-primary); }
  .guide-page h3 { font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; margin: 1.25rem 0 0.5rem; }
  .guide-page p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .guide-page ul, .guide-page ol { margin: 0 0 0.75rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .guide-page li { margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .guide-page strong { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .guide-page a { color: var(--accent); }
  .formula-inline { font-family: var(--font-mono); background: var(--bg-tertiary); padding: 0.75rem 1rem; border-radius: var(--radius-md); display: block; margin: 0.75rem 0; font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--accent); }
  .guide-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.8rem; }
  .guide-table th, .guide-table td { padding: 0.5rem 0.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--border-primary); text-align: left; }
  .guide-table th { background: var(--bg-tertiary); font-weight: 600; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .guide-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: var(--bg-secondary); }
  .guide-nav { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; margin-top: 2rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-primary); }
  .btn-primary, .btn-secondary { padding: 0.625rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 600; border-radius: var(--radius-md); cursor: pointer; transition: all var(--transition); border: 1px solid transparent; text-decoration: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg-primary); border-color: var(--accent); }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--accent-hover); border-color: var(--accent-hover); color: var(--bg-primary); text-decoration: none; }
  .btn-secondary { background: transparent; color: var(--text-secondary); border-color: var(--border-secondary); }
  .btn-secondary:hover { color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
</style>